module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.AssociatedPrime.Finiteness
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.TensorProduct.Finite
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.TameSymbol.FiniteExtension
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.TameSymbol.Independence
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Ideal.AssociatedPrime.MaximalPowerTorsion
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Localization.SemilocalizationFibre

/-!
# The common refinement of two finite modifications

Let `(A, 𝔪)` be a one-dimensional Noetherian local ring. The formula Stacks 0EAQ for the tame
symbol is computed over a finite ring extension `A ⊆ B` with `B / A` annihilated by a power of
`𝔪` and `𝔪` not an associated prime of `B` — the extensions Stacks 0EAG produces. Stacks 0EAR
asserts that the value does not depend on that extension, and its proof compares two extensions
`B` and `B'`, neither refining the other, through a third one refining both:

`C = (B ⊗_A B') / (𝔪-power torsion)`.

This file constructs `C` and proves that it is an extension of the same kind, that `B` and `B'`
both map into it, and that the three properties localize to the fibre over each maximal ideal of
`B` — which is the form in which the refinement case of Stacks 0EAR consumes them.

Every one of the three global properties rests on one device. A power `𝔪 ^ n'` of the maximal
ideal moves `B'` into `A`, and `A → B'` is injective, so multiplication by `y ∈ 𝔪 ^ n'` on `B'`
factors through a genuine `A`-linear map `f : B' → A` with `algebraMap (f x) = y • x`. Tensoring
`f` with the identity of `B` and composing with `B ⊗_A A ≅ B` gives an `A`-linear map
`B ⊗_A B' → B` carrying `b ⊗ 1` to `y • b`. Hence `𝔪 ^ n'` kills the kernel of `B → B ⊗_A B'`,
and symmetrically `𝔪 ^ n` kills the kernel of `B' → B ⊗_A B'`. Since `B`, `B'` and `A` have no
`𝔪`-power torsion, every one of `A`, `B` and `B'` maps injectively into `C`. That `𝔪 ^ (n + n')`
annihilates `C / A` is the computation `(x y) • (b ⊗ b') = (x • b) ⊗ (y • b')` with both factors
in the image of `A`, and that `𝔪` is not an associated prime of `C` is exactly what dividing by
the torsion achieves.

The fibre statements are the same three properties for `B_𝔮 ⊆ C_𝔮`, where `C_𝔮` is the
semilocalization of `C` at a maximal ideal `𝔮` of `B`. Injectivity localizes directly. For the
other two the point is that `𝔪` and `𝔮 B_𝔮` have the same powers up to cofinality: a power of
the maximal ideal of `B_𝔮` lies in `𝔪 B_𝔮`, because the only prime of `B_𝔮` containing `𝔪 B_𝔮`
is the maximal one — a prime of `B` below `𝔮` and over `𝔪` is maximal, hence equal to `𝔮`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Chow.TorsionCommonRefinement` — `(B ⊗_A B') / (𝔪`-power torsion`)`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.not_isAssociatedPrime_commonRefinement` — `𝔪` is not an associated prime of the
  common refinement.
* `Stacks.Chow.injective_algebraMap_commonRefinement`,
  `Stacks.Chow.injective_algebraMap_left_commonRefinement`,
  `Stacks.Chow.injective_algebraMap_right_commonRefinement` — `A`, `B` and `B'` all map
  injectively into the common refinement.
* `Stacks.Chow.exists_pow_smul_le_range_commonRefinement` — a power of `𝔪` annihilates the
  quotient of the common refinement by `A`.
* `Stacks.Chow.maximalIdeal_pow_le_map_maximalIdeal` — a power of the maximal ideal of the local
  ring of a finite extension at a maximal ideal lies in the ideal generated by `𝔪`.
* `Stacks.Chow.not_isAssociatedPrime_semilocalization`,
  `Stacks.Chow.exists_pow_smul_le_range_semilocalization` — two of the three properties at the
  fibre over a maximal ideal of `B`, for an arbitrary extension `C` of the same kind; the third,
  injectivity, is `Stacks.Chow.injective_algebraMap_semilocalization` of
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.TameSymbol.Independence`.
* `Stacks.Chow.injective_algebraMap_semilocalization_commonRefinement`,
  `Stacks.Chow.not_isAssociatedPrime_semilocalization_commonRefinement`,
  `Stacks.Chow.exists_pow_smul_le_range_semilocalization_commonRefinement` and their `_right`
  counterparts — the same three properties for the common refinement, over a maximal ideal of
  `B` and over a maximal ideal of `B'`, which is the shape in which the refinement case of
  Stacks 0EAR consumes them.
* `Stacks.Chow.exists_mem_maximalIdeal_mem_nonZeroDivisors` — the maximal ideal of a Noetherian
  local ring that is not an associated prime of the ring contains a nonzerodivisor.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EAR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EAR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EAG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EAG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EAQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EAQ)
-/

@[expose] public section

open IsLocalRing TensorProduct

universe u v w

namespace Stacks.Chow

/-! ### Multiplication by an element of `𝔪 ^ n` on a tensor factor -/

section Factor

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {B : Type v} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
  {B' : Type w} [CommRing B'] [Algebra A B'] {I : Ideal A} {n : ℕ}

/-- If `y • M ⊆ A` and `A → M` is injective, multiplication by `y` on `M` factors through an
`A`-linear map `M → A` sending `1` to `y`. -/
private theorem exists_linearMap_apply_one_eq {M : Type*} [CommRing M] [Algebra A M]
    (hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap A M))
    (hquot : I ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule A M) ≤ LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A M))
    {y : A} (hy : y ∈ I ^ n) : ∃ f : M →ₗ[A] A, f 1 = y := by
  have hmem : ∀ x : M, (LinearMap.lsmul A M y) x ∈ LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A M) :=
    fun x => hquot (Submodule.smul_mem_smul hy Submodule.mem_top)
  have hinjl : Function.Injective (Algebra.linearMap A M) := hinj
  refine ⟨LinearMap.codRestrictOfInjective (LinearMap.lsmul A M y)
    (Algebra.linearMap A M) hinjl hmem, hinj ?_⟩
  exact (LinearMap.codRestrictOfInjective_comp_apply (LinearMap.lsmul A M y)
    (Algebra.linearMap A M) hinjl hmem 1).trans (by simp [Algebra.smul_def])

/-- **Multiplication by an element of an ideal annihilating `B' / A` factors the tensor product
through `B`.** If `y • B' ⊆ A` and `A → B'` is injective, multiplication by `y` on `B'` is
`algebraMap` composed with an `A`-linear map `f : B' → A`; tensoring `f` with the identity of `B`
and contracting `B ⊗_A A ≅ B` sends `b ⊗ 1` to `(f 1) • b = y • b`. So an element of `B` whose
image in `B ⊗_A B'` vanishes is killed by `y`. -/
theorem smul_eq_zero_of_tmul_one_eq_zero (hinj' : Function.Injective (algebraMap A B'))
    (hquot' : I ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule A B') ≤ LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A B'))
    {y : A} (hy : y ∈ I ^ n) {b : B} (hb : (b ⊗ₜ[A] (1 : B') : B ⊗[A] B') = 0) :
    y • b = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨f, hf1⟩ := exists_linearMap_apply_one_eq hinj' hquot' hy
  calc y • b
      = (TensorProduct.rid A B)
          (TensorProduct.map (LinearMap.id : B →ₗ[A] B) f (b ⊗ₜ[A] (1 : B'))) := by
        simp [hf1]
    _ = 0 := by rw [hb, map_zero, map_zero]

/-- **Multiplication by an element of an ideal annihilating `B / A` factors the tensor product
through `B'`**, the mirror image of `Stacks.Chow.smul_eq_zero_of_tmul_one_eq_zero`. -/
theorem smul_eq_zero_of_one_tmul_eq_zero (hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap A B))
    (hquot : I ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule A B) ≤ LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A B))
    {y : A} (hy : y ∈ I ^ n) {b' : B'} (hb' : ((1 : B) ⊗ₜ[A] b' : B ⊗[A] B') = 0) :
    y • b' = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨f, hf1⟩ := exists_linearMap_apply_one_eq hinj hquot hy
  calc y • b'
      = (TensorProduct.lid A B')
          (TensorProduct.map f (LinearMap.id : B' →ₗ[A] B') ((1 : B) ⊗ₜ[A] b')) := by
        simp [hf1]
    _ = 0 := by rw [hb', map_zero, map_zero]

end Factor

/-! ### The common refinement -/

section Definition

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] (B : Type v) [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
  (B' : Type w) [CommRing B'] [Algebra A B']

/-- **The common refinement of two finite modifications of `A`**, namely
`(B ⊗_A B') / (𝔪`-power torsion`)`. Both `B` and `B'` map to it, and when `B` and `B'` are
finite extensions of a one-dimensional Noetherian local ring with `𝔪`-power torsion cokernel and
with `𝔪` not an associated prime, so is this. -/
def TorsionCommonRefinement : Type (max v w) :=
  (B ⊗[A] B') ⧸ Stacks.primaryComponentIdeal A (B ⊗[A] B') (maximalIdeal A)

/-- The `𝔪`-power torsion ideal the common refinement is the quotient by. -/
abbrev commonRefinementIdeal : Ideal (B ⊗[A] B') :=
  Stacks.primaryComponentIdeal A (B ⊗[A] B') (maximalIdeal A)

/-- The common refinement is a commutative ring, as a quotient of `B ⊗[A] B'`. -/
instance : CommRing (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B') :=
  inferInstanceAs (CommRing ((B ⊗[A] B') ⧸ commonRefinementIdeal A B B'))

/-- The common refinement is a `B ⊗[A] B'`-algebra via the quotient map. -/
instance : Algebra (B ⊗[A] B') (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B') :=
  inferInstanceAs (Algebra (B ⊗[A] B') ((B ⊗[A] B') ⧸ commonRefinementIdeal A B B'))

/-- The common refinement is an `A`-algebra. -/
instance : Algebra A (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B') :=
  inferInstanceAs (Algebra A ((B ⊗[A] B') ⧸ commonRefinementIdeal A B B'))

/-- The common refinement is a `B`-algebra via the left-hand factor. -/
instance : Algebra B (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B') :=
  inferInstanceAs (Algebra B ((B ⊗[A] B') ⧸ commonRefinementIdeal A B B'))

/-- The `A`-algebra structure of the common refinement factors through `B ⊗[A] B'`. -/
instance : IsScalarTower A (B ⊗[A] B') (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B') :=
  inferInstanceAs (IsScalarTower A (B ⊗[A] B')
    ((B ⊗[A] B') ⧸ commonRefinementIdeal A B B'))

/-- The `A`-algebra structure of the common refinement factors through `B`. -/
instance : IsScalarTower A B (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B') :=
  inferInstanceAs (IsScalarTower A B ((B ⊗[A] B') ⧸ commonRefinementIdeal A B B'))

/-- The quotient map of the common refinement. -/
def mkCommonRefinement : (B ⊗[A] B') →+* TorsionCommonRefinement A B B' :=
  Ideal.Quotient.mk (commonRefinementIdeal A B B')

/-- The quotient map onto the common refinement is surjective. -/
theorem mkCommonRefinement_surjective :
    Function.Surjective (mkCommonRefinement A B B') :=
  Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective

/-- An element of `B ⊗[A] B'` maps to zero in the common refinement if and only if it is
`𝔪`-power torsion. -/
theorem mkCommonRefinement_eq_zero_iff {d : B ⊗[A] B'} :
    mkCommonRefinement A B B' d = 0 ↔ d ∈ commonRefinementIdeal A B B' :=
  Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem

/-- The algebra map from `B ⊗[A] B'` to the common refinement is the quotient map. -/
theorem algebraMap_tensor_eq_mk :
    algebraMap (B ⊗[A] B') (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B') = mkCommonRefinement A B B' := rfl

/-- The structure map of the right-hand factor into the common refinement. -/
def includeRightHom : B' →+* TorsionCommonRefinement A B B' :=
  (mkCommonRefinement A B B').comp
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight (R := A) (A := B) (B := B')).toRingHom

/-- The common refinement is a `B'`-algebra via the right-hand factor. -/
instance : Algebra B' (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B') := (includeRightHom A B B').toAlgebra

/-- The algebra map from `B'` to the common refinement sends `b'` to the class of `1 ⊗ b'`. -/
theorem algebraMap_right_apply (b' : B') :
    algebraMap B' (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B') b' =
      mkCommonRefinement A B B' ((1 : B) ⊗ₜ[A] b') := rfl

/-- The `A`-algebra structure of the common refinement factors through `B'`. -/
instance : IsScalarTower A B' (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B') :=
  IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun a => by
    rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A (B ⊗[A] B') (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B') a,
      algebraMap_right_apply]
    exact congrArg (mkCommonRefinement A B B')
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight.commutes a).symm

end Definition

section Finite

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] (B : Type v) [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
  [Module.Finite A B] (B' : Type w) [CommRing B'] [Algebra A B'] [Module.Finite A B']

/-- If `B` and `B'` are finite over `A`, so is the common refinement. -/
instance : Module.Finite A (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B') :=
  Module.Finite.of_surjective
    (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ A (commonRefinementIdeal A B B')).toLinearMap
    fun z => by
      obtain ⟨d, rfl⟩ := mkCommonRefinement_surjective A B B' z
      exact ⟨d, rfl⟩

/-- If `B` and `B'` are finite over `A`, the common refinement is finite over `B`. -/
instance : Module.Finite B (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B') :=
  Module.Finite.of_restrictScalars_finite A B (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B')

/-- If `B` and `B'` are finite over `A`, the common refinement is finite over `B'`. -/
instance : Module.Finite B' (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B') :=
  Module.Finite.of_restrictScalars_finite A B' (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B')

end Finite

/-! ### The common refinement is an extension of the same kind -/

section Properties

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
  {B : Type v} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] {B' : Type w} [CommRing B'] [Algebra A B']

omit [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsLocalRing A] in
/-- An `A`-scalar multiple of a residue class is the class of the scalar multiple. -/
private theorem smul_algebraMap {D E : Type*} [CommRing D] [CommRing E] [Algebra A D]
    [Algebra D E] [Algebra A E] [IsScalarTower A D E] (a : A) (d : D) :
    a • (algebraMap D E d) = algebraMap D E (a • d) := by
  rw [Algebra.smul_def, Algebra.smul_def, map_mul, IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A D E]

/-- **`𝔪` is not an associated prime of the common refinement.** This is exactly what dividing
the tensor product by its `𝔪`-power torsion achieves. -/
theorem not_isAssociatedPrime_commonRefinement :
    ¬ IsAssociatedPrime (maximalIdeal A) (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B') :=
  Stacks.not_isAssociatedPrime_maximalIdeal_quotient_primaryComponentIdeal A (B ⊗[A] B')

omit [IsNoetherianRing A] in
/-- **`𝔪` is not an associated prime of `A` itself** when it is not one of a faithful
modification: an associated prime of `A` stays one along an injective `A`-linear map. -/
theorem not_isAssociatedPrime_self (hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap A B))
    (hB : ¬ IsAssociatedPrime (maximalIdeal A) B) :
    ¬ IsAssociatedPrime (maximalIdeal A) A :=
  fun h => hB (h.map_of_injective (f := Algebra.linearMap A B) hinj)

omit [IsNoetherianRing A] in
/-- **A power of `𝔪` annihilates `(B ⊗_A B') / A`.** If `𝔪 ^ n` moves `B` into `A` and `𝔪 ^ n'`
moves `B'` into `A`, then `(x y) • (b ⊗ b') = (x • b) ⊗ (y • b')` has both factors in the image
of `A`, hence is itself in the image of `A`. -/
theorem pow_smul_tensor_le_range {n n' : ℕ}
    (hquot : maximalIdeal A ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule A B) ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A B))
    (hquot' : maximalIdeal A ^ n' • (⊤ : Submodule A B') ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A B')) :
    maximalIdeal A ^ (n + n') • (⊤ : Submodule A (B ⊗[A] B')) ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A (B ⊗[A] B')) := by
  rw [Submodule.smul_le]
  intro r hr
  rw [pow_add] at hr
  refine Submodule.mul_induction_on hr ?_ ?_
  · intro x hx y hy z _
    induction z using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
    | tmul u v =>
        obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hquot (Submodule.smul_mem_smul hx (Submodule.mem_top (x := u)))
        obtain ⟨c', hc'⟩ := hquot' (Submodule.smul_mem_smul hy (Submodule.mem_top (x := v)))
        have hcu : x • u = algebraMap A B c := hc.symm
        have hcv : y • v = algebraMap A B' c' := hc'.symm
        refine ⟨c * c', ?_⟩
        change algebraMap A (B ⊗[A] B') (c * c') = (x * y) • (u ⊗ₜ[A] v)
        rw [mul_smul, ← TensorProduct.tmul_smul, TensorProduct.smul_tmul', hcu, hcv,
          Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one (R := A) (A := B) c,
          Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one (R := A) (A := B') c',
          Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one (R := A) (A := B ⊗[A] B') (c * c'),
          Algebra.TensorProduct.one_def, mul_smul, ← TensorProduct.tmul_smul,
          TensorProduct.smul_tmul']
    | add z z' hz hz' =>
        rw [smul_add]
        exact Submodule.add_mem _ (hz Submodule.mem_top) (hz' Submodule.mem_top)
  · intro r r' hr hr' z hz
    rw [add_smul]
    exact Submodule.add_mem _ (hr z hz) (hr' z hz)

omit [IsNoetherianRing A] in
/-- **A power of `𝔪` annihilates `C / A` for the common refinement `C`.** -/
theorem exists_pow_smul_le_range_commonRefinement {n n' : ℕ}
    (hquot : maximalIdeal A ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule A B) ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A B))
    (hquot' : maximalIdeal A ^ n' • (⊤ : Submodule A B') ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A B')) :
    ∃ N : ℕ, maximalIdeal A ^ N • (⊤ : Submodule A (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B')) ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B')) := by
  refine ⟨n + n', ?_⟩
  rw [Submodule.smul_le]
  intro r hr z _
  obtain ⟨d, rfl⟩ := mkCommonRefinement_surjective A B B' z
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := pow_smul_tensor_le_range hquot hquot'
    (Submodule.smul_mem_smul hr (Submodule.mem_top (x := d)))
  refine ⟨c, ?_⟩
  rw [Algebra.linearMap_apply] at hc
  change algebraMap A (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B') c =
    r • algebraMap (B ⊗[A] B') (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B') d
  rw [smul_algebraMap, IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A (B ⊗[A] B')
    (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B') c]
  exact congrArg (algebraMap (B ⊗[A] B') (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B')) hc

/-- An element `b` of a module without `𝔪` as an associated prime vanishes if `x • y • b = 0`
for all `x ∈ 𝔪 ^ n` and `y ∈ 𝔪 ^ k`. -/
private theorem eq_zero_of_pow_smul_pow_smul_eq_zero {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M]
    (hM : ¬ IsAssociatedPrime (maximalIdeal A) M) {n k : ℕ} {b : M}
    (h : ∀ x ∈ maximalIdeal A ^ n, ∀ y ∈ maximalIdeal A ^ k, x • y • b = 0) : b = 0 := by
  refine Stacks.eq_zero_of_mem_primaryComponent hM
    (Stacks.mem_primaryComponent_of_pow_smul_eq_zero (k := n + k) fun z hz => ?_)
  rw [pow_add] at hz
  refine Submodule.mul_induction_on hz (fun x hx y hy => ?_) fun z z' hz hz' => ?_
  · rw [mul_smul]
    exact h x hx y hy
  · rw [add_smul, hz, hz', add_zero]

/-- **`B` maps injectively into the common refinement.** A power of `𝔪` kills the kernel of
`B → B ⊗_A B'`, and the class of `b` vanishes only if a power of `𝔪` moves `b ⊗ 1` into the
torsion; so `b` is `𝔪`-power torsion in `B`, hence zero. -/
theorem injective_algebraMap_left_commonRefinement
    (hinj' : Function.Injective (algebraMap A B'))
    (hB : ¬ IsAssociatedPrime (maximalIdeal A) B) {n' : ℕ}
    (hquot' : maximalIdeal A ^ n' • (⊤ : Submodule A B') ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A B')) :
    Function.Injective (algebraMap B (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B')) := by
  refine (injective_iff_map_eq_zero (algebraMap B (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B'))).mpr
    fun b hb => ?_
  have hb' : mkCommonRefinement A B B' (b ⊗ₜ[A] (1 : B')) = 0 := hb
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := Stacks.mem_primaryComponent_iff.mp
    ((mkCommonRefinement_eq_zero_iff A B B').mp hb')
  refine eq_zero_of_pow_smul_pow_smul_eq_zero hB (n := n') (k := k) fun x hx y hy => ?_
  refine smul_eq_zero_of_tmul_one_eq_zero hinj' hquot' hx ?_
  rw [← TensorProduct.smul_tmul']
  exact hk y hy

/-- **`B'` maps injectively into the common refinement**, the mirror image of
`Stacks.Chow.injective_algebraMap_left_commonRefinement`. -/
theorem injective_algebraMap_right_commonRefinement
    (hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap A B))
    (hB' : ¬ IsAssociatedPrime (maximalIdeal A) B') {n : ℕ}
    (hquot : maximalIdeal A ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule A B) ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A B)) :
    Function.Injective (algebraMap B' (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B')) := by
  refine (injective_iff_map_eq_zero (algebraMap B' (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B'))).mpr
    fun b' hb => ?_
  have hb' : mkCommonRefinement A B B' ((1 : B) ⊗ₜ[A] b') = 0 := hb
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := Stacks.mem_primaryComponent_iff.mp
    ((mkCommonRefinement_eq_zero_iff A B B').mp hb')
  refine eq_zero_of_pow_smul_pow_smul_eq_zero hB' (n := n) (k := k) fun x hx y hy => ?_
  refine smul_eq_zero_of_one_tmul_eq_zero hinj hquot hx ?_
  rw [TensorProduct.tmul_smul]
  exact hk y hy

/-- **`A` maps injectively into the common refinement.** -/
theorem injective_algebraMap_commonRefinement
    (hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap A B)) (hinj' : Function.Injective (algebraMap A B'))
    (hB : ¬ IsAssociatedPrime (maximalIdeal A) B) {n' : ℕ}
    (hquot' : maximalIdeal A ^ n' • (⊤ : Submodule A B') ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A B')) :
    Function.Injective (algebraMap A (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B')) := by
  rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq A B (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B')]
  exact (injective_algebraMap_left_commonRefinement hinj' hB hquot').comp hinj

/-- **The maximal ideal of a Noetherian local ring that is not an associated prime of the ring
contains a nonzerodivisor.** Were every element of `𝔪` a zerodivisor, `𝔪` would lie in the union
of the finitely many associated primes of `A`, hence in one of them, hence be equal to it. -/
theorem exists_mem_maximalIdeal_mem_nonZeroDivisors
    (hass : ¬ IsAssociatedPrime (maximalIdeal A) A) :
    ∃ x ∈ maximalIdeal A, x ∈ nonZeroDivisors A := by
  by_contra hcon
  obtain ⟨P, hP, hle⟩ :=
    ((maximalIdeal A).subset_union_prime_finite (associatedPrimes.finite A A) (f := id) 0 0
      fun _ h _ _ => h.1).1 (by
        simp_rw [id, biUnion_associatedPrimes_eq_compl_nonZeroDivisors A]
        exact fun x hx hmem => hcon ⟨x, hx, hmem⟩)
  refine hass ?_
  rw [(maximalIdeal.isMaximal A).eq_of_le
    (AssociatedPrimes.mem_iff.mp hP).isPrime.ne_top hle]
  exact hP

end Properties

/-! ### The three properties at the fibre over a maximal ideal of `B` -/

section Fibre

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A]
  {B : Type v} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [Module.Finite A B]
  {C : Type w} [CommRing C] [Algebra B C] [Algebra A C] [IsScalarTower A B C]
  (q : MaximalSpectrum B)

omit [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A] [Module.Finite A B] in
/-- The two routes from `A` to the semilocalization of `C` at `𝔮` agree: through `B_𝔮` and
through `C`. There is no scalar-tower instance for `A → B_𝔮 → C_𝔮`, so the identity is spelled
out along `A → B → B_𝔮 → C_𝔮` and `A → B → C → C_𝔮`. -/
theorem algebraMap_semilocalization_algebraMap (x : A) :
    algebraMap (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)
        (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl))
        (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal) x) =
      algebraMap C (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl))
        (algebraMap A C x) := by
  rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A B (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal),
    ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply B (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)
      (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl)),
    IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply B C
      (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl)),
    ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A B C]

omit [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A] in
/-- **A power of the maximal ideal of `B_𝔮` lies in the ideal generated by `𝔪`.** The only prime
of `B_𝔮` containing `𝔪 B_𝔮` is the maximal one: a prime of `B` below `𝔮` whose contraction to
`A` contains `𝔪` lies over `𝔪`, hence is maximal because `B` is integral over `A`, hence equals
`𝔮`. So the maximal ideal of `B_𝔮` is inside the radical of `𝔪 B_𝔮`, and a finitely generated
ideal inside a radical has a power inside the ideal. -/
theorem maximalIdeal_pow_le_map_maximalIdeal :
    ∃ M : ℕ, maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal) ^ M ≤
      Ideal.map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)) (maximalIdeal A) := by
  have hBq : IsNoetherianRing (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal) :=
    IsLocalization.isNoetherianRing q.asIdeal.primeCompl _ (IsNoetherianRing.of_finite A B)
  refine Ideal.exists_pow_le_of_le_radical_of_fg ?_ (IsNoetherian.noetherian _)
  rw [Ideal.radical_eq_sInf]
  refine le_sInf fun p hp => ?_
  obtain ⟨hJp, hpp⟩ := hp
  have hpp' : p.IsPrime := hpp
  have hcomap : (p.under B).under A =
      Ideal.comap (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)) p := by
    rw [Ideal.under, Ideal.under, Ideal.comap_comap,
      ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq A B (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)]
  have hmle : maximalIdeal A ≤ (p.under B).under A := by
    rw [hcomap]
    exact fun a ha => hJp (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha)
  have hprime : ((p.under B).under A).IsPrime := by
    rw [hcomap]
    infer_instance
  have hmax : ((p.under B).under A).IsMaximal :=
    (maximalIdeal.isMaximal A).eq_of_le hprime.ne_top hmle ▸ maximalIdeal.isMaximal A
  have hqmax : (p.under B).IsMaximal :=
    Ideal.isMaximal_of_isIntegral_of_isMaximal_under (R := A) (p.under B) hmax
  have hle : p.under B ≤ q.asIdeal := by
    have h : p.under B ≤ (maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)).under B :=
      Ideal.comap_mono (IsLocalRing.le_maximalIdeal hpp.ne_top)
    rwa [IsLocalization.AtPrime.under_maximalIdeal _ q.asIdeal] at h
  have hpq : p.under B = q.asIdeal := hqmax.eq_of_le q.isMaximal.ne_top hle
  calc maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)
      = Ideal.map (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)) q.asIdeal :=
        Localization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal.symm
    _ = Ideal.map (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)) (p.under B) := by rw [hpq]
    _ ≤ p := Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr le_rfl

omit [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A] in
/-- **`𝔪` and the maximal ideal of `B_𝔮` have the same powers up to cofinality**: the image of
`𝔪 ^ N` generates an ideal of `B_𝔮` containing a power of the maximal ideal. -/
theorem maximalIdeal_pow_le_map_maximalIdeal_pow (N : ℕ) :
    ∃ n : ℕ, maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal) ^ n ≤
      Ideal.map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)) (maximalIdeal A ^ N) := by
  obtain ⟨M, hM⟩ := maximalIdeal_pow_le_map_maximalIdeal (A := A) q
  refine ⟨M * N, ?_⟩
  rw [pow_mul, Ideal.map_pow]
  exact pow_le_pow_left' hM N

omit [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A] in
/-- **A power of the maximal ideal of `B_𝔮` annihilates `C_𝔮 / B_𝔮`.** An element `a` of `𝔪 ^ N`
carries `c / s` to `(a • c) / s`, whose numerator is in the image of `A`; writing `s` as the image
of `b ∈ B \ 𝔮` exhibits the result as the image of an element of `B_𝔮`. A power of the maximal
ideal of `B_𝔮` lies in the ideal `𝔪 ^ N` generates, which finishes the argument because the image
of `B_𝔮` is a `B_𝔮`-submodule. -/
theorem exists_pow_smul_le_range_semilocalization {N : ℕ}
    (hquot : maximalIdeal A ^ N • (⊤ : Submodule A C) ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A C)) :
    ∃ n : ℕ, maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal) ^ n •
        (⊤ : Submodule (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)
          (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl))) ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)
        (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl))) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := maximalIdeal_pow_le_map_maximalIdeal_pow (A := A) q N
  refine ⟨n, ?_⟩
  have hstep : ∀ a ∈ maximalIdeal A ^ N,
      ∀ z : Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl),
        (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal) a) • z ∈
          LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)
            (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl))) := by
    intro a ha z
    obtain ⟨⟨c, s⟩, rfl⟩ := IsLocalization.mk'_surjective
      (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl) z
    obtain ⟨b, hb, hbs⟩ := s.2
    obtain ⟨c₀, hc₀⟩ := hquot (Submodule.smul_mem_smul ha (Submodule.mem_top (x := c)))
    refine ⟨IsLocalization.mk' (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal) (algebraMap A B c₀) ⟨b, hb⟩, ?_⟩
    have hs : (⟨algebraMap B C b, Algebra.mem_algebraMapSubmonoid_of_mem (⟨b, hb⟩ :
        q.asIdeal.primeCompl)⟩ : Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl) = s :=
      Subtype.ext hbs
    have hlhs : Algebra.linearMap (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)
          (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl))
            (IsLocalization.mk' (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal) (algebraMap A B c₀) ⟨b, hb⟩) =
        IsLocalization.mk' (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl))
          (algebraMap A C c₀) s := by
      rw [Algebra.linearMap_apply, IsLocalization.algebraMap_mk' (S := C), hs,
        ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A B C]
    have hrhs : (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal) a) •
          IsLocalization.mk' (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl))
            c s =
        IsLocalization.mk' (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl))
          (algebraMap A C c₀) s := by
      rw [Algebra.smul_def, algebraMap_semilocalization_algebraMap q a,
        IsLocalization.mul_mk'_eq_mk'_of_mul]
      congr 1
      rw [Algebra.linearMap_apply, Algebra.smul_def] at hc₀
      exact hc₀.symm
    rw [hlhs, hrhs]
  refine le_trans (Submodule.smul_mono_left hn) ?_
  rw [Submodule.smul_le]
  intro r hr z _
  have hK : Ideal.map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)) (maximalIdeal A ^ N) ≤
      (LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)
        (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl)))).colon Set.univ :=
    Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun a ha =>
      Submodule.mem_colon.mpr fun z _ => hstep a ha z
  exact Submodule.mem_colon.mp (hK hr) z (Set.mem_univ z)

/-- **`𝔪_𝔮` is not an associated prime of the semilocalization of `C` at `𝔮`.** A nonzerodivisor
`x` of `A` inside `𝔪` stays a nonzerodivisor in `C`, hence in the semilocalization, and its image
lies in the maximal ideal of `B_𝔮`; so an element of `C_𝔮` killed by a power of `𝔪_𝔮` is killed by
a power of a nonzerodivisor and vanishes. -/
theorem not_isAssociatedPrime_semilocalization
    (hC : ¬ IsAssociatedPrime (maximalIdeal A) C)
    {x : A} (hxm : x ∈ maximalIdeal A) (hx : x ∈ nonZeroDivisors A) :
    ¬ IsAssociatedPrime (maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal))
      (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl)) := by
  have hBq : IsNoetherianRing (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal) :=
    IsLocalization.isNoetherianRing q.asIdeal.primeCompl _ (IsNoetherianRing.of_finite A B)
  have hlocal : IsLocalHom (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)) :=
    Stacks.Length.isLocalHom_algebraMap_localization q
  have hxBq : algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal) x ∈
      maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal) :=
    (mem_maximalIdeal _).mpr fun h =>
      (mem_maximalIdeal x).mp hxm (isUnit_of_map_unit _ x h)
  have hxCq : algebraMap C (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl))
      (algebraMap A C x) ∈
      nonZeroDivisors (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl)) :=
    IsLocalization.map_nonZeroDivisors_le (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl)
      (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C q.asIdeal.primeCompl))
      ⟨algebraMap A C x, mem_nonZeroDivisors_algebraMap hC hx, rfl⟩
  refine Stacks.not_isAssociatedPrime_maximalIdeal_of_forall_eq_zero fun z hz => ?_
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := Stacks.mem_primaryComponent_iff.mp hz
  have hpow := hk _ (Ideal.pow_mem_pow hxBq k)
  rw [Algebra.smul_def, map_pow, algebraMap_semilocalization_algebraMap q x] at hpow
  exact mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_left.mp (pow_mem hxCq k) z hpow

end Fibre

/-! ### The three properties of the common refinement, at the fibre over a maximal ideal of `B` -/

section CommonRefinementFibre

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A]
  {B : Type v} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [Module.Finite A B]
  {B' : Type w} [CommRing B'] [Algebra A B'] [Module.Finite A B']
  (q : MaximalSpectrum B)

omit [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A] [Module.Finite A B] [Module.Finite A B'] in
/-- **`B_𝔮` maps injectively into the semilocalization of the common refinement at `𝔮`.** -/
theorem injective_algebraMap_semilocalization_commonRefinement
    (hinj' : Function.Injective (algebraMap A B'))
    (hB : ¬ IsAssociatedPrime (maximalIdeal A) B) {n' : ℕ}
    (hquot' : maximalIdeal A ^ n' • (⊤ : Submodule A B') ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A B')) :
    Function.Injective (algebraMap (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)
      (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B')
        q.asIdeal.primeCompl))) :=
  injective_algebraMap_semilocalization
    (injective_algebraMap_left_commonRefinement hinj' hB hquot') q

omit [Module.Finite A B'] in
/-- **The maximal ideal of `B_𝔮` is not an associated prime of the semilocalization of the common
refinement at `𝔮`.** -/
theorem not_isAssociatedPrime_semilocalization_commonRefinement
    (hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap A B))
    (hB : ¬ IsAssociatedPrime (maximalIdeal A) B) :
    ¬ IsAssociatedPrime (maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal))
      (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B')
        q.asIdeal.primeCompl)) := by
  obtain ⟨x, hxm, hx⟩ :=
    exists_mem_maximalIdeal_mem_nonZeroDivisors (not_isAssociatedPrime_self hinj hB)
  exact not_isAssociatedPrime_semilocalization q
    (not_isAssociatedPrime_commonRefinement (B := B) (B' := B')) hxm hx

omit [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A] [Module.Finite A B'] in
/-- **A power of the maximal ideal of `B_𝔮` annihilates the quotient of the semilocalization of
the common refinement at `𝔮` by `B_𝔮`.** -/
theorem exists_pow_smul_le_range_semilocalization_commonRefinement {n n' : ℕ}
    (hquot : maximalIdeal A ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule A B) ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A B))
    (hquot' : maximalIdeal A ^ n' • (⊤ : Submodule A B') ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A B')) :
    ∃ m : ℕ, maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal) ^ m •
        (⊤ : Submodule (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)
          (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B')
            q.asIdeal.primeCompl))) ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap (Localization.AtPrime q.asIdeal)
        (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B')
          q.asIdeal.primeCompl))) := by
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := exists_pow_smul_le_range_commonRefinement hquot hquot'
  exact exists_pow_smul_le_range_semilocalization q hN

omit [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A] [Module.Finite A B] [Module.Finite A B'] in
/-- **`B'_𝔮` maps injectively into the semilocalization of the common refinement at a maximal
ideal `𝔮` of `B'`.** -/
theorem injective_algebraMap_semilocalization_commonRefinement_right
    (q' : MaximalSpectrum B') (hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap A B))
    (hB' : ¬ IsAssociatedPrime (maximalIdeal A) B') {n : ℕ}
    (hquot : maximalIdeal A ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule A B) ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A B)) :
    Function.Injective (algebraMap (Localization.AtPrime q'.asIdeal)
      (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B')
        q'.asIdeal.primeCompl))) :=
  injective_algebraMap_semilocalization
    (injective_algebraMap_right_commonRefinement hinj hB' hquot) q'

omit [Module.Finite A B] in
/-- **The maximal ideal of `B'_𝔮` is not an associated prime of the semilocalization of the
common refinement at a maximal ideal `𝔮` of `B'`.** -/
theorem not_isAssociatedPrime_semilocalization_commonRefinement_right
    (q' : MaximalSpectrum B') (hinj' : Function.Injective (algebraMap A B'))
    (hB' : ¬ IsAssociatedPrime (maximalIdeal A) B') :
    ¬ IsAssociatedPrime (maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q'.asIdeal))
      (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B')
        q'.asIdeal.primeCompl)) := by
  obtain ⟨x, hxm, hx⟩ :=
    exists_mem_maximalIdeal_mem_nonZeroDivisors (not_isAssociatedPrime_self hinj' hB')
  exact not_isAssociatedPrime_semilocalization q'
    (not_isAssociatedPrime_commonRefinement (B := B) (B' := B')) hxm hx

omit [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A] [Module.Finite A B] in
/-- **A power of the maximal ideal of `B'_𝔮` annihilates the quotient of the semilocalization of
the common refinement at a maximal ideal `𝔮` of `B'` by `B'_𝔮`.** -/
theorem exists_pow_smul_le_range_semilocalization_commonRefinement_right
    (q' : MaximalSpectrum B') {n n' : ℕ}
    (hquot : maximalIdeal A ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule A B) ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A B))
    (hquot' : maximalIdeal A ^ n' • (⊤ : Submodule A B') ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap A B')) :
    ∃ m : ℕ, maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q'.asIdeal) ^ m •
        (⊤ : Submodule (Localization.AtPrime q'.asIdeal)
          (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B')
            q'.asIdeal.primeCompl))) ≤
      LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap (Localization.AtPrime q'.asIdeal)
        (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (TorsionCommonRefinement A B B')
          q'.asIdeal.primeCompl))) := by
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := exists_pow_smul_le_range_commonRefinement
    (B := B) (B' := B') hquot hquot'
  exact exists_pow_smul_le_range_semilocalization q' hN

end CommonRefinementFibre

end Stacks.Chow

end
